{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And a man who lies with a woman.</b> Rabbi Elazar ben Azariah says: all the forbidden relations have already been stated; we have only this one — she who is half slave-woman and half free woman." "<b>Designated.</b> Betrothed, as in 'in the days of my betrothal,' 'in the days of my designation.' Another interpretation: abandoned, 'abandonée' in the vernacular, as in 'a people that exposes itself to death.'" "<b>Free.</b> The heh is weak (rafeh)." "<b>There shall be an inquiry.</b> An expression of inquiry: they shall investigate and examine her circumstances — how it is that <b>they shall not be put to death</b> if <b>she was not freed</b> — as Rashi explained."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:33.476290580Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}